# #1974 (P21a): a `for` target is block-scoped, so the outer x survives the loop; a `let x` in a
# later block is fresh again — 100 / 7 / 100. The write-through reading would print 100 / 7 / 7.
def main():
    x = 100
    for x in [1, 2, 3]:
        pass
    print(x)
    if True:
        let x = 7
        print(x)
    print(x)
